WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.726
Imagine you sell cupcakes at a school fair for two dollars each, and you sell forty. You receive two times forty, which is eighty dollars. That money is your revenue.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:26.242
Pay works the same way. Remuneration is the total reward paid to employees. If you earn ten dollars an hour for six hours, your pay is sixty dollars.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:36.696
Step one, find the rate: the price per item, or the pay per hour. For revenue, always use the selling price, not a cost.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:49.545
Step two, find every quantity. Watch the time period. Five sales every month for a year means five times twelve. If there are several shops or factories, add them together first.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:57.639
Step three, multiply the rate by the total quantity. Step four, write the currency and round as asked.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:15.126
Here is a real question from Paper one in November 2024, about a robot maker in Türkiye. Each battery pack sells for ninety dollars, and it sold five every month in 2023. Calculate the total revenue for the year.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:22.347
The rate is ninety dollars per pack. In one month, revenue is ninety times five, which is four hundred and fifty dollars.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:32.851
There are twelve months in a year. Four hundred and fifty times twelve is five thousand four hundred dollars. Or, sixty packs times ninety dollars gives the same.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:44.958
The most common mistake is stopping at one month. Four hundred and fifty dollars is only one month. The question asked for the whole year.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:55.989
Another mistake is multiplying only one group. If two shops each sell goods, add both shops' sales before you multiply by the price.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:13.518
Now you try. A café employs three workers. Each works twenty-five hours a week at eight dollars fifty an hour. Calculate the café's total weekly pay. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:22.966
First, the total quantity. Three workers each work twenty-five hours, so that is seventy-five hours a week.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:31.040
Now multiply by the rate. Seventy-five times eight dollars fifty is six hundred and thirty-seven dollars fifty a week.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:39.434
Remember the method: find the rate, find every quantity including the time period, then multiply. Now try the practice questions.
